        {
          "turn": 1,
          "speaker": "Cary",
          "text": "Can you hold the end of the tape measure at the fireplace? I want the width from both walls before I touch the roll."
        },
        {
          "turn": 2,
          "speaker": "Fiona",
          "text": "Got it. You already checked this side once, you know."
        },
        {
          "turn": 3,
          "speaker": "Cary",
          "text": "[weary sigh] Once with the furniture still in here, and once with the room clear. This carpet cost too much to guess at."
        },
        {
          "turn": 4,
          "speaker": "Fiona",
          "text": "[overwhelmed sob] It actually fits. After all those weekends of looking at samples, I can finally picture us sitting in here."
        },
        {
          "turn": 5,
          "speaker": "Cary",
          "text": "[choked sob] I kept promising we'd finish this room after the leak, and then work kept getting in the way. Hand me the straightedge, and I'll make the cut."
        },
        {
          "turn": 6,
          "speaker": "Fiona",
          "text": "Here. The marks line up exactly with your measurements."
        },
        {
          "turn": 7,
          "speaker": "Cary",
          "text": "Good. Keep the roll from shifting while I guide the knife along this edge."
        },
        {
          "turn": 8,
          "speaker": "Fiona",
          "text": "It's clean all the way across. Let's lay it down before the backing curls up again."
        },
        {
          "turn": 9,
          "speaker": "Cary",
          "text": "[exhausted sigh] There, the far corner is tucked under. I just need to press this tape firmly along the seam."
        },
        {
          "turn": 10,
          "speaker": "Fiona",
          "text": "[sigh of relief] No gaps, no crooked edge, and it reaches the fireplace perfectly. It looks better than the sample did."
        },
        {
          "turn": 11,
          "speaker": "Cary",
          "text": "[relieved sob] We did it. Go ahead and step onto it first; this room finally feels like ours."
        },
        {
          "turn": 12,
          "speaker": "Fiona",
          "text": "It feels wonderful. I’ll bring in the sofa cushions, and tonight we can actually use the living room."
