      "turns": [
        {
          "turn": 1,
          "speaker": "Aminah",
          "text": "I finally finished my blog post about today—the library book sale, the rain, and finding Dad's old map in the donation box."
        },
        {
          "turn": 2,
          "speaker": "John",
          "text": "You actually opened that box? You've been moving it around the kitchen for months."
        },
        {
          "turn": 3,
          "speaker": "Aminah",
          "text": "I did. I wrote about tracing the faded trail lines and deciding the youth hiking club could use it more than my cupboard could."
        },
        {
          "turn": 4,
          "speaker": "John",
          "text": "That sounds like a good day to write about: useful, a little messy, and honest."
        },
        {
          "turn": 5,
          "speaker": "Aminah",
          "text": "[reflective sigh] I almost made the whole thing into a joke, but I wrote that the kitchen felt occupied again while I held the map."
        },
        {
          "turn": 6,
          "speaker": "John",
          "text": "[moved sob] That line got me. It lets him be present without pretending nothing has changed."
        },
        {
          "turn": 7,
          "speaker": "Aminah",
          "text": "[warm laughter] You are supposed to be proofreading, not turning my comments section into a puddle. Did the ending work?"
        },
        {
          "turn": 8,
          "speaker": "John",
          "text": "Yes. Giving the map away lands well, especially when you mention the club's thank-you note."
        },
        {
          "turn": 9,
          "speaker": "Aminah",
          "text": "[relieved sob] I included the part where they promised to mark their first trail with it. That made letting go feel less like losing it."
        },
        {
          "turn": 10,
          "speaker": "John",
          "text": "[fond laughter] Look at you calling that a note after you framed it beside the coffee maker. Keep that detail in; it is completely you."
        },
        {
          "turn": 11,
          "speaker": "Aminah",
          "text": "[sigh of relief] I hit publish. Somehow I feel peaceful now, like I put the day where it belongs."
        },
        {
          "turn": 12,
          "speaker": "John",
          "text": "Then leave it there tonight. Tomorrow, you can tell me whether anyone from the hiking club reads it."
        }
      ],
